WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:03.220
(crowd cheering enthusiastically)

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:05.480
- [Jonathan] China celebrated
the 100th anniversary

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:08.283
of its ruling Communist party on July 1st.

00:00:08.283 --> 00:00:10.260
(cannons banging)

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:11.960
This anniversary is really a moment

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:14.130
for the Chinese Communist
Party to be able to look back

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:16.320
on how far it's come, from a party

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:19.060
that was more or less ruled
out as a potential power player

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:21.010
into the driving force behind the country

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:23.580
that is now the world's
second largest economy

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.380
and on pace to be its number-one economy.

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:28.400
Xi Jinping really wants
to take this moment

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.468
and say China has arrived.

00:00:30.468 --> 00:00:34.468
(Xi speaks in foreign language)

00:00:42.006 --> 00:00:45.173
(audience applauding)

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:58.523
- [Jonathan] Nobody thought

00:00:58.523 --> 00:01:01.000
that the CCP would be this successful

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:04.160
when it was founded in 1921,
whether it be in science,

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:06.950
technology, in sports and the economy.

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:09.230
In almost every facet, China is stronger

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:11.380
than it's been in the
past and, in a sense,

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:12.960
they're really gonna give

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:15.040
the U.S. and the West a run for its money.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:17.220
- We're in a race with China and the rest

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:18.980
of the world for the 21st century.

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:21.980
They're not waiting, they're
investing tens of billions

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:23.680
of dollars across the board.

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:25.020
- But to surpass the U.S.,

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:27.805
China will have to overcome
several challenges.

00:01:27.805 --> 00:01:29.870
(people murmuring)

00:01:29.870 --> 00:01:31.900
This is a time when China's
economy is recovering

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:34.650
from the coronavirus pandemic
earlier than everywhere else

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:36.550
and that's left China
looking pretty strong.

00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:39.940
Its economy is expected
to grow by 8.5% this year,

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:42.250
and it was gaining ground
not only in the U.S.,

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:44.030
but it was adding ground

00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:46.673
between itself and many of its neighbors.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:50.280
It was able to take advantage
of the demand for exports

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:53.000
all around the world
when people needed PPE,

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.990
when people needed medical equipment,

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:57.410
when people needed computer equipment.

00:01:57.410 --> 00:01:59.570
It's made big leaps in mobile payments,

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:02.520
artificial intelligence,
quantum computing,

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:04.599
and even sending a rover to Mars.

00:02:04.599 --> 00:02:07.000
(triumphant music)

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.080
So part of the strength
of the Chinese state

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:12.640
over the last 30 to 40 years
has been based on its economy.

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:17.120
It's grown so quickly and
with a massive population

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:19.470
it had both a large base of labor

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:23.050
as well as a huge market
for Western companies

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:25.050
and other foreign companies
to move into China.

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:27.130
What we're starting to
see now is that some

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:30.020
of that economic growth is
slowing, mainly you have

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:33.160
a population in China that
is skewing older and older.

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:34.730
Chinese demographers believe

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:38.720
that China really has about
a 10, 15-year window here

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:41.270
before things start to
get really bad in terms

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:43.990
of the number of people
that you have working,

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:47.810
trying to support X number
of people who are retired.

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:50.430
So one of the measures that the
Chinese government has taken

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:53.410
was to allow Chinese
people to have more babies.

00:02:53.410 --> 00:02:57.270
That's because for the better
part of the last four decades

00:02:57.270 --> 00:03:01.250
China has restricted most
families to only having one child.

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:02.450
(guns banging)

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:04.620
One of the most important
priorities for Xi Jinping

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:07.440
has been ensuring that
China's periphery is secure.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:09.900
It has Xinjiang, it has Hong Kong,

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:11.990
and we've seen very strong
controls put in place there

00:03:11.990 --> 00:03:13.550
over the past few years
to really make sure

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:16.090
that Beijing's will is first and foremost.

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:18.470
Beijing has drawn global
scrutiny for its use

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:20.090
of surveillance technology to keep an eye

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:22.743
on people's activities in
Xinjiang and Hong Kong.

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:25.590
Beijing has said that
national security concerns

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:26.770
in Hong Kong have required it

00:03:26.770 --> 00:03:28.990
to take stronger measures in the city.

00:03:28.990 --> 00:03:31.270
Chinese authorities have
defended the use of surveillance

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:33.210
in Xinjiang as designed to promote

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:35.360
development and security for locals.

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:36.270
- They have an overall goal

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:38.840
to become the leading
country in the world,

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:39.753
the wealthiest country in the world,

00:03:39.753 --> 00:03:41.903
and the most powerful
country in the world.

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:45.113
That's not gonna happen on my watch.

00:03:45.113 --> 00:03:47.230
- [Jonathan] Biden's rhetoric
has actually been very tough

00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:49.170
since he became president and he has said

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:52.610
that genocide is what is
happening in Xinjiang.

00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:56.520
- DHS is deeply concerned by
credible and growing reports

00:03:56.520 --> 00:04:00.120
of China's state-sponsored
use of forced labor

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:04.033
and other human rights violations
in the Xinjiang region.

00:04:04.033 --> 00:04:08.283
(Zhao speaks in foreign language)

00:04:21.622 --> 00:04:24.740
- Biden has said that, in
contrast to his predecessor,

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:27.430
he wants to work with other
democracies to stand up

00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:29.340
to autocratic governments like China's.

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:32.910
It seems like in Washington
Biden has now reflected

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:34.850
and captured the zeitgeist there

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:38.450
that says China is
fundamentally different from us

00:04:38.450 --> 00:04:41.630
in terms of their values and
they're gaining ground on us

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:44.510
in a way that we should
be very worried about.

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:48.020
Over the next 10 to 15 years,
Xi has made it very clear

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:50.590
that he wants to build self-sufficiency.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:52.410
I think he's recognized
that China's too reliant

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:54.900
in some ways on the West in
areas like semiconductors

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:57.150
and technologies with
military applications,

00:04:57.150 --> 00:05:00.140
and China is definitely
doing things in its own way.

00:05:00.140 --> 00:05:03.180
It's stepped up control of big
and powerful tech companies,

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:05.760
such as the fintech giant
Ant and how it handles

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:07.483
the user data that it generates.

00:05:07.483 --> 00:05:11.566
(Xi speaks in foreign language)

00:05:25.899 --> 00:05:29.120
- [Jonathan] What Xi Jinping
says and wants is for China

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:31.520
to be able to keep its prosperity

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:35.890
but also be more ideologically committed

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:39.700
to the Communist underpinning
that first inspired

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:41.945
the founders of the Communist
Party here in China.

00:05:41.945 --> 00:05:43.370
(audience applauding)

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:46.710
He also wants a country
where the people are gonna be

00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:48.990
more loyal to China than
they have been in the past.

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:51.657
(gentle music)

